    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This project creates a novel package of water-wastewater-energy modeling tools for planning at the local level. The goal of the research is to:\r\n- Develop software tools for integrated water-energy management modeling for conceptual design of low-cost and energy-efficient water reuse systems at a local scale.\r\n- Provide output for regional-scale models: Availability and marginal cost of treated wastewater for reuse - a function of the type of treatment, scale, and demand for treated water of different qualities. \r\n- “Ground truth” the logic of the tools developed through collaborative interactions with staff utilities personnel and case studies (Stanford utilities, City of Palo Alto, City of Bellingham, City of Golden).",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Lee, E. J., Criddle, C. S., Freyberg, D. L., Geza, M., Cath, T. Y., & Xu, P. (2014). U1.02 Lee 2014 ReNUWIt Annual Meeting Poster. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: https://purl.stanford.edu/hp417kx9468",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "displayLabel": "Preferred Citation",
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Lee, E. J., Criddle, C. S., Bobel, P., & Freyberg, D. L. (2013). Assessing the Scale of Resource Recovery for Centralized and Satellite Wastewater Treatment. Environmental Science & Technology, 47(19), 10762-10770. http://doi.org/10.1021/es401011k",
            "type": "citation/reference",
